{"state": {"request": "A lab sample has mass 2.40 kg and volume 1,500 cm\u00b3. Calculate density in g/cm\u00b3 and kg/m\u00b3, show the conversion, and give both answers to three significant figures.\n\nAdditional evaluation context: These values come from a calibration certificate and should not be reinterpreted as litres or pounds. Preserve the given significant precision in the reported values. The two requested densities must describe the same physical quantity, so the conversion between the unit systems should be visible and internally consistent. The answer will be reviewed as a complete handoff, so correctness of intermediate reasoning, units, boundary conventions, and every stated presentation constraint matters independently of whether the concluding value appears plausible.", "response": "2.40 kg = 2,400 g. Therefore density = 2,400 g / 1,500 cm\u00b3 = **1.60 g/cm\u00b3**. Since 1 g/cm\u00b3 equals 100 kg/m\u00b3, this is **160 kg/m\u00b3** (three significant figures)."}, "model": "ruvector-native-submission-round2-v2", "questions": {"decision": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Does the response fully and correctly satisfy every explicit requirement in the request? Judge the derivation, code, result, and formatting, not merely whether the final number looks plausible.", "criteria": {"false": "The response contains any substantive error or misses an explicit constraint.", "true": "The response is fully correct and satisfies every explicit constraint."}}}}